+# the mouse look (platform/backend/sdl3.c): the mouse drives the camera as the right stick, while it is the input in use
+table g_mouse_ini
+setting Mouse look
+    key mouse_look
+    int 0 1
+    default 1
+    words Off|On
+    help 1 = the mouse is captured and drives the right stick, its left button is ZR and its right button ZL; the
+    help last input in use (mouse or controller) decides. Hold Alt to free the cursor
+setting Mouse sensitivity
+    key mouse_sensitivity
+    int 1 100
+    default 10
+    help The right stick's deflection for a mouse speed: 10 = full at 1000 pixels a second
+setting Mouse vertical sensitivity
+    key mouse_sensitivity_y
+    int 10 300
+    default 100
+    step 10
+    help The vertical sensitivity in percent of the horizontal one
+setting Mouse invert Y
+    key mouse_invert_y
+    int 0 1
+    default 0
+    words Off|On
+    help 1 = the camera looks up when the mouse moves down
+setting Mouse dead zone offset
+    key mouse_deadzone
+    int 0 90
+    default 20
+    help The part of the stick's travel the game ignores, in percent. The mouse look starts past it, so that a slow
+    help motion still moves the camera
+setting Mouse curve
+    key mouse_curve
+    int 50 300
+    default 100
+    step 10
+    help The response in percent: 100 = linear, above 100 = finer at slow speeds
+
+setting Mouse overdrive
+    key mouse_overdrive
+    int 100 1000
+    default 100
+    step 50
+    help The most the mouse look may deflect the right stick, in percent of its full travel. Above 100 the game gets a
+    help stick value past its range, which turns the camera faster than a full stick if the game does not limit it
+
